The request is closed. What I did, and what I found:

**Verified result written** under section 4 of `/home/vscode/rebaseline/requests/req-2026-09-06-plain-status.md` (new `### Verified result` subsection, after `### Check`, before Document History). It records:
- the verifying observation the Definition named (the lint-plus-grep command, run from the repository root);
- its evidence as captured — the two lint lines, the grep hits at line 33 (the added rule) and line 65 (the guideline's history row citing this request), and the closing `exit 0`;
- the date (2026-09-09) and my role (lead-pm, at the small-change lane's verify step);
- that the Definition, the Check's pass verdict by the lead-pm role (round 1), and this result stand; and that between the request and this result no bet was taken and no check of record was run — the small-change lane carries neither.

**Frontmatter:** `status` routed → done; `version` 5 → 6; `updated` 2026-09-09. **Document History:** row 6 added describing the above. Lint passes (0 violations) after the write.

**On the heading-duplication note from the prior step:** confirmed. `read --section` returns the `## ...` heading line as its first line, and `write --part` places content under the heading it keeps — so a naive read-append-write doubles the heading. I stripped the heading line from each read before appending and writing back; the file has exactly one `## 4. Result` and one `## Document History`. One further tool quirk worth passing on: `write --part updated --content "'2026-09-09'"` produced `'''2026-09-09'''` — the tool adds its own YAML quoting, so frontmatter string values should be passed bare. I corrected it in place.

Nothing was committed; the working tree also carries uncommitted changes from earlier steps in this session (the guideline, two other requests, features, an initiative), which I left untouched.

